Notebook[{
Cell["InfraVolume", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"014c19b8-dae3-417e-ae66-4366690f0f21"],

Cell["[LLM Generated]", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"4c046fa4-39d5-445c-96b7-825777566a7d"],

Cell["\<\
InfraVolume[g, s] is the volume of s (a bare vertex list or any Infra* \
object) in g. Option \"Volume\" (\"Hausdorff\" (default), |s| minus its \
boundary; \"Counting\", |s|; \"Boundary\", the boundary count). For set-like \
s (InfraSet, InfraBall, InfraShell, ...) the boundary is the inner vertex \
boundary of the union vertex set (Method \"Combinatorial\" (default) or \
{\"Alexandrov\", \"Radius\" -> r}, shared with InfraBoundary / \
InfraInterior). For line-like s (InfraLine, InfraSegment, InfraPath, \
InfraRay) the graph is the union of the walks as path graphs (line edges \
only, so distinct lines are not joined), and a vertex is interior iff all its \
g-edges are line edges -- a curve in a higher-dimensional graph has ~empty \
interior even when it spans the whole graph.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0a71940f-5c26-49db-8313-95d6a34a8a47"],

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d100dfb9-dcc7-4198-8778-1b1fe87efe27"],

Cell["Load the paclet.", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"f3053ff3-8511-4ede-b434-caca4950d78e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<WolframInstitute`SyntheticInfrageometry`\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "Code",
 InitializationCell->
  True,ExpressionUUID->"82a84b2e-610a-4b57-b712-8d68c33467c6"],

Cell["Related Guides", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b170143d-5d55-4032-8bf3-875c19d7b5bb"],

Cell["EuclideanGeometryGuide", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"a1c071bc-a5b4-437b-b850-8448a00df839"],

Cell["SyntheticInfrageometryGuide", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"8245abd7-9ea1-44e9-b1a4-3cfa32c260a1"]
},
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Mac OS X ARM (64-bit) (May 19, 2026)",
